  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "695b4fd2-9f78-46e5-9097-1bc15582e743",
    "name": "Ghost Content and Admin APIs Admin - Images Admin - Pages API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Ghost is an open-source (MIT) publishing platform for professional publications, newsletters, memberships, and paid subscriptions. Every Ghost site - whether self-hosted or on managed Ghost(Pro) - exposes two documented public REST APIs under https://{admin_domain}/ghost/api/.\n\nThe Content API is read-only and is authenticated with a Content API key passed as the `key` query parameter; it serves published posts, pages, authors, tags, tiers, and public settings for consumption by front-ends and static sites.\n\nThe Admin API is read-write and is authenticated with an Admin API key that is used to sign a short-lived JWT sent as `Authorization: Ghost {token}` (a staff access token or user session may also be used). It manages posts, pages, members, tags, labels, tiers, offers, newsletters, users, images, themes, and webhooks.\n\nThe `{admin_domain}` server variable is the site's domain (for Ghost(Pro), typically a `*.ghost.io` domain). All requests must use HTTPS. The `Accept-Version` header (for example `v5.0`) declares the minimum compatible API version.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Ghost",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
